            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Chay - Thực Dưỡng Quỳnh House",
            "review_text": "Albert N\n1 contribution\n0\nA wonderful night out\nApr 2023 • Friends\n4/5 for this eatery experience! From the moment I walked in, I was impressed by the warm and inviting atmosphere. The decor was modern yet comfortable, and the staff greeted me with smiles and enthusiasm.\n\nI had a dish called “Nem Vuong”. Apparently it is noodles and mushrooms wrapped in a deep fried layer of rice paper. The waitress told me it was a traditional dish in North Vietnam. For the taste, it was smoky, delicious, and especially not oily. I would say this is one of their must-try dish.\n\nMy friend ordered the laksa and oh boy I'd say I regretted not ordering it earlier. The vegetarian laksa was the star of the show. It was cooked with fiery and flavorful curry broth made from spicy herbs and coconut milk. They topped it with a yummy egg with various vegetables (if you are strict ethical/religious vegans do order vegan laksa, they'll just remove the eggs) \n\nAnother dish I had was the house-made veggie patties with vermicelli noodles. It was a bit dry but the flavor was well-balanced with fresh ingredients.\n\nA feature that not many vegetarian restaurants have which I can’t get enough of is their buffet. It serves you delicious bread and colorful jelly. On top of that, it’s free. \n\nThis restaurant is one of the most affordable restaurants out there that not only serves luxurious dishes for a reasonable price, but also great service, great food, and gorgeous design.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 19, 2023\nQuỳnh House - Vegetarian Restaurant\nThank you for visitng Quynh House Vegetarian Dining! We're always delighted to serve you and dear ones.\nWritten April 20, 2023\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
